{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/776428-silver-fang-celestial-lodges","id":776428,"title":"Silver Fang Celestial Lodges","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-28T22:24:06-08:00","id":776428,"title":"Silver Fang Celestial Lodges","content":"I'm looking for input on the details of the Silver Fang lodges. After reading the tribebooks, they seem organized per SF Royal House. So while lodge members can be anywhere, the activities seem mostly limited to advising the SF kings in their home septs and implementing his policies among the tribe.<br /> <br /> However, they also hold big seasonal solstice moots. Does that mean the Silver Fangs of each House gather at their king's sept? I think while that could happen, that the tribe also meets at the local septs or perhaps regional septs most of the time. The logistics of bringing the entire tribe (per royal house) together at one sept twice every year seems excessive and unlikely. Although if there are very important reasons for the entire royal house to meet, they would do so. I could also see some sort of &quot;big&quot; solstice moot that does happen at the King's sept, but which may only be done every ten years or so.<br /> <br /> If you've roleplayed one of the big lodge solstice moots, how did your game do it?<br /> <br /> I'll likely be running a solstice moot soon for my SF PCs. Rather than holding it at the king's sept (which I haven't designed), I'm saying the tribe gathers at several locations in order to make it convenient for most tribe members. I can then introduce some of the tribal NPCs, but not include the entire royal house they belong to. I haven't done much with the Lodges, but I want to include them more in my chronicle to help the PCs develop their characters and become more involved in the tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T04:54:20-08:00","id":776519,"title":"","content":"Sadly my players do not like playing Silver Fangs so I haven't had the need to deal with the lodges.<br /> However I have written a chronicle with the lodges acting as a sort of backer/employer I used both soltices and equinoxes as times of ceremony at the Silver Fang Sept. The Lodge of the Moon ran the Summer Solstice celebration. The Lodge of the Sun the Winter. Both lodges ran the equinoxes celebration rites. The pack was not present for the rites as they were basically on guard duty. If you want to have characters joining the lodges I would have them recruited to assist in the rite. Perhaps during the story portion for the Galliard with the other characters taking on roles in the story being told.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}